    "assertions": "Dirty constructor reopen, blocked ordinary mutation, no read/stale-GC repair, generation-checked authoritative GC, valid H and full physical pre-delete floor checkpoint before physical orphan deletion, durable second reopen. Covers masked negative size, unsafe/fractional size/peak/fallback, exact SQLite INT_MAX SUM overflow, 1,025 individually safe values with overflowing total, empty invalid fallback replacement, and loss of every historical witness."
  },
  "historical_limit": "Recovery preserves max(all still-valid durable historical witnesses, process floor, entire physical pre-delete inventory). If every trustworthy historical witness was corrupted/lost, an arbitrary older peak is unknowable. The lost-witness regression recovers actual physical floor170 rather than inventing old H500. This is distinct from the documented R11 unrecorded-upload crash gap.",
